sum='Arunima Sinha, a national-level volleyball player from Ambedkar Nagar (Uttar Pradesh), lost a leg in a train accident on 11 April 2011 at the age of 24. Lying in hospital, she vowed not only to walk again with a prosthetic leg but to climb Mount Everest. She did a basic mountaineering course at the Nehru Institute of Mountaineering, Uttarkashi, and 18 months of rigorous training, guided by Bachendri Pal (first Indian woman to summit Everest), who told her she had already “conquered the Everest within” her. On 21 May 2013, after 52 exhausting days, she reached the summit, displayed the Indian flag and left a photograph of her idol Swami Vivekananda. She went on to climb the highest peaks of other continents and, in January 2019, Mount Vinson in Antarctica, completing the Seven Summits. She received the Padma Shri (2015), the Tenzing Norgay National Adventure Award and an honorary doctorate (University of Strathclyde). Her autobiography is “Born Again on the Mountain”. Her message: never give up, work hard, and always remember your goal.',
